#version 450
#extension GL_GOOGLE_include_directive : require
// Ray-traced diffuse GI (the two-space gather pass): STRATIFIED
// cosine-distributed hemisphere rays per pixel, each ray resolved in TWO
// spaces exactly like Lumen - marched through the SCREEN-SPACE depth buffer
// first (the rasterized truth: meshes and analytic primitives at per-pixel
// fidelity), with the EXACT analytic scene SDF as the world-space fallback -
// hit points relit with their textured materials, one screen-space second
// bounce, and a reprojection-validated temporal accumulation.
//
// Rev 33 (the research round): every stage of the pass is CONFIGURABLE, each
// knob mapped onto the control Unreal exposes for the same stage (the
// mapping was verified against Epic's documentation and the SIGGRAPH 2022
// Lumen course notes - see README.md and FINDINGS.md round 33):
//   screen_trace            ~ r.Lumen.ScreenProbeGather.ScreenTraces (the
//                             Post Process "Screen Traces" checkbox)
//   screen_steps            ~ r.Lumen.ScreenProbeGather.ScreenTraces.
//                             HZBTraversal.MaxIterations (trace budget)
//   screen_max_distance     ~ Post Process "Max Trace Distance", screen half
//   screen_thickness        ~ the linear-step thickness tolerance (the leak
//                             guard Lumen's HZB traversal replaces)
//   temporal_max_frames     ~ r.Lumen.ScreenProbeGather.Temporal.
//                             MaxFramesAccumulated (default 10; ours 64)
//   temporal_normal_rejection ~ Lumen's depth+normal history rejection
//   short_range_ao_radius   ~ r.Lumen.ScreenProbeGather.ShortRangeAO (the
//                             16 px "shortest range occlusion" band)
//   rays_per_pixel          ~ the final-gather quality dial (Lumen tunes the
//                             probe octahedron resolution instead)
//   intensity / sky_miss_scale ~ the output-shaping pair
//
// The pass fills the renderer's indirectRadiance target with the unit the
// composite expects: irradiance / pi (the composite multiplies albedo into
// it). With cosine-weighted sampling the estimator for E/pi is simply the
// mean of the incoming radiance over the rays - no extra weights.
//
// Why this shape mirrors Lumen (and where it deliberately differs):
//   Lumen surface cache  -> the analytic relight (relight_common.glsl): every
//                           hit point is shaded with the SAME textured direct
//                           lighting the G-buffer pass rasterizes with. This
//                           is Lumen's "hit lighting" material answer, not
//                           its card-based surface cache - our field IS the
//                           geometry, so no card capture exists to replace.
//   Lumen final gather   -> the cosine hemisphere gather, resolved in TWO
//                           spaces (rev 32). DELIBERATE DIFFERENCE: Lumen
//                           gathers at 1/16-resolution screen PROBES and
//                           interpolates (probes exist to amortize tracing
//                           across pixels); we gather per pixel and spend
//                           the budget on rays instead. Same ordering, same
//                           reason: indirect shadows at pixel fidelity.
//   Lumen screen trace   -> the screen march below: linear exponential
//                           strides + bisect. Lumen walks hierarchical-Z
//                           mips instead (linear steps skip thin occluders);
//                           our thickness tolerance plays the same leak-guard
//                           role at this buffer's resolution.
//   Lumen radiance cache -> the previous frame's gathered irradiance sampled
//                           at the hit point's reprojection (a two-bounce
//                           approximation that costs one texture fetch).
//                           Lumen's two-level probe hierarchy is the full
//                           answer; the one-fetch memory is what a per-pixel
//                           gather can afford.
//   Temporal accumulation -> reprojection-validated history blend, depth +
//                           normal rejection, a running-average ramp CAPPED
//                           by temporal_max_frames (Lumen's
//                           MaxFramesAccumulated: an uncapped ramp hardens
//                           into a frozen average that stops tracking the
//                           scene).
//   Short-range AO       -> the post-temporal screen-space occlusion ring
//                           (Lumen applies its shortest-range occlusion
//                           AFTER the temporal filter so it carries no lag).
//
// Rev 31 (the owner's "this GI is noisy"): the estimator went from one
// ray to giPush.params.z STRATIFIED rays per pixel - each ray's two jitter
// draws get their own golden-ratio-rotated offset, decorrelating the samples
// inside one pixel the way the temporal ramp decorrelates frames - and every
// ray's radiance passes the indirect clamp (params.w): rare hits on the
// emissive panel or a lamp no longer print as un-filterable specks. The
// frame-0 guard stops the blend from mixing the fresh estimate into an
// UNDEFINED history image (the rev-30 first-frame initialization bug).
//
// The alpha channel of the output carries the pixel's view depth (distance
// camera -> shaded point). The reprojection confidence for BOTH the pixel's
// own history and the second-bounce fetch compares that stored depth against
// the distance the reprojection predicts, which disocclusions and silhouettes
// fail and flat surfaces pass.

// The flat-albedo relight switch: the capture reference rasterizer crashes
// executing arrayed texture fetches inside compute kernels (see
// materials_common.glsl, ENGINE_RELIGHT_FLAT_ALBEDO). The bounce albedo is
// the primitive's palette tint + ALU variation; the GI chamber's flat
// materials are exact under it.
#define ENGINE_RELIGHT_FLAT_ALBEDO
#include "scene_common.glsl"
#include "relight_common.glsl"
#include "environment_common.glsl"

layout(local_size_x = 8, local_size_y = 8, local_size_z = 1) in;

layout(set = 1, binding = 0) uniform sampler2D albedoSampler; // rgb albedo, a roughness (unused: relight re-derives)
layout(set = 1, binding = 1) uniform sampler2D normalSampler; // rgb world normal, a metallic
layout(set = 1, binding = 2) uniform sampler2D depthSampler;
layout(set = 1, binding = 3, rgba16f) uniform restrict writeonly image2D giImage;
layout(set = 1, binding = 4) uniform sampler2D historySampler; // rgb last frame's irradiance/pi, a view depth

// Last frame's camera (the reprojection source). The pass uploads it from
// its own host copy each record BEFORE the dispatch, then stores the current
// camera after the dispatch - the shader therefore always reprojects with
// the previous frame's matrices, never the current ones.
layout(std140, set = 0, binding = 7) uniform PreviousCameraUniform
{
    mat4 viewProjection;
    mat4 inverseViewProjection;
    vec4 cameraPosition;
} previousCamera;

layout(push_constant) uniform GiPush
{
    layout(offset = 0) uvec4 counts;   // x primitive count, y frame index, z world march steps, w second bounce (0/1)
    layout(offset = 16) vec4 params;   // x max trace distance, y temporal alpha floor, z rays per pixel, w indirect clamp
    layout(offset = 32) vec4 params2;  // x screen strides, y screen thickness (m), z screen march bound (m), w screen bisect steps
    layout(offset = 48) uvec4 flags;   // x screen traces 0/1, y animated jitter 0/1, z temporal normal rejection 0/1, w short-range AO radius (px)
    layout(offset = 64) vec4 params3;  // x temporal ramp cap (frames), y short-range AO strength, z intensity, w sky-miss scale
    layout(offset = 80) vec4 params4;  // x spatial filter radius (px; the denoise dispatch reads this), y-z-w reserved
} giPush;

// Interleaved gradient noise (Jimenez): the per-pixel, per-frame jitter that
// decorrelates the ray directions between neighbours and frames. The
// temporal blend turns the noise into convergence; a static camera sees the
// estimator average down, a moving camera sees film-grain-level residual.
// animated_jitter = 0 freezes the frame phase (flags.y) - the noise stays
// constant across frames, which makes a capture reproducible frame for
// frame (the A/B harness pins it off).
float interceptNoise(vec2 pixel, float frame)
{
    return fract(52.9829189 * fract(0.06711056 * pixel.x + 0.00583715 * pixel.y + 0.0857 * frame));
}

// Right-handed ONB around an arbitrary unit normal (Duff's method): branch-
// free, no cross products, stable for every normal including +/-Y.
void onb(vec3 n, out vec3 tangent, out vec3 bitangent)
{
    const float s = n.z >= 0.0 ? 1.0 : -1.0;
    const float a = -1.0 / (s + n.z);
    const float b = n.x * n.y * a;
    tangent   = vec3(1.0 + s * n.x * n.x * a, s * b, -s * n.x);
    bitangent = vec3(b, s + n.y * n.y * a, -n.y);
}

// Reprojection of a world point into the PREVIOUS frame's screen uv, or
// vec2(-1.0) when the point falls outside the previous frustum.
vec2 previousUv(vec3 worldPoint)
{
    const vec4 clip = previousCamera.viewProjection * vec4(worldPoint, 1.0);
    if (clip.w <= 0.0)
    {
        return vec2(-1.0);
    }
    const vec2 uv = clip.xy / clip.w * 0.5 + 0.5;
    if (uv.x < 0.0 || uv.x > 1.0 || uv.y < 0.0 || uv.y > 1.0)
    {
        return vec2(-1.0);
    }
    return uv;
}

// Reprojection confidence: the previous frame stored the view depth of the
// surface it shaded there; the reprojected point predicts a depth. Flat
// continuation passes (relative error small), silhouettes and disocclusions
// fail (the stored depth jumps). The band scales with the depth so distant
// geometry is not held to a centimetre tolerance.
//
// temporal_normal_rejection (flags.z, Lumen's depth+normal history
// rejection): the depth test alone passes a flat wall that has SLID across
// the pixel under motion; the second term rejects history where the
// G-buffer normal at the reprojected uv disagrees with the shaded normal
// (an 8th-power cosine - a tight cone, same shape the spatial filter uses).
float historyConfidence(vec2 uv, float predictedDepth, vec3 shadedNormal, float normalRejection)
{
    const vec4 history = texture(historySampler, uv);
    if (history.a <= 0.0 || history.a >= 30000.0)
    {
        return 0.0; // sky pixel last frame (the 60000 sentinel): no surface history
    }
    const float band = max(0.35, 0.12 * predictedDepth);
    float confidence = exp(-abs(history.a - predictedDepth) / band);
    if (normalRejection > 0.5)
    {
        const vec3 historyNormal = normalize(texture(normalSampler, uv).xyz);
        confidence *= pow(max(dot(shadedNormal, historyNormal), 0.0), 8.0);
    }
    return confidence;
}

// ---- the screen-space stage (rev 32, the Lumen ordering's first half) ----
// The ray is marched through THIS frame's depth buffer before the analytic
// SDF is consulted. Everything here is the rasterized truth - mesh instances
// and analytic primitives alike - at per-pixel fidelity: silhouettes are
// exact even where the world trace would graze an occluder proxy, the hit's
// material is the one the G-buffer actually shaded, and the march carries no
// jitter, so near-field bounces add no estimator noise. Distances are
// compared Euclidean-from-the-camera (no view-space dependency): a sample has
// crossed a buffered surface when its camera distance exceeds the buffer
// pixel's by more than the thickness tolerance.
//
// Rev 33: stride count, bisect depth, thickness tolerance and march bound
// all arrive through the push block (screen_steps / screen_refine /
// screen_thickness / screen_max_distance), and the whole stage is skippable
// (screen_trace = 0: the world-only A/B, Lumen's Screen Traces off).

bool screenMarch(vec3 origin, vec3 direction, uint primitiveCount,
                 float maxDistance, uint strideSteps, uint refineSteps,
                 float thickness, out vec3 hitPoint, out vec2 hitUv, out vec3 hitNormal)
{
    hitPoint = vec3(0.0);
    hitUv = vec2(0.0);
    hitNormal = vec3(0.0, 1.0, 0.0);
    const float tMax = min(maxDistance, giPush.params2.z);
    const float stepMin = 0.05; // the first stride: 5 cm contact-band precision
    float tPrev = 0.0;
    bool prevInFront = true; // the origin rides its own surface by 2 cm
    for (uint step = 0u; step < strideSteps; ++step)
    {
        // Exponential stride: 5 cm at the first step, the spacing growing
        // until the march reaches tMax - near-field detail is what the
        // screen stage exists for.
        const float t = stepMin * pow(tMax / stepMin, float(step + 1) / float(strideSteps));
        const vec3 samplePoint = origin + direction * t;
        const vec4 clip = viewProjection * vec4(samplePoint, 1.0);
        if (clip.w <= 0.0)
        {
            return false; // behind the camera: the screen cannot answer
        }
        const vec2 sampleUv = clip.xy / clip.w * 0.5 + 0.5;
        if (any(lessThan(sampleUv, vec2(0.0))) || any(greaterThan(sampleUv, vec2(1.0))))
        {
            return false; // off the screen: the world stage takes over
        }
        const float bufferDepth = texture(depthSampler, sampleUv).r;
        const vec3 bufferPoint = worldPositionFromDepth(inverseViewProjection,
                                                        sampleUv * 2.0 - vec2(1.0), bufferDepth);
        const float bufferDistance = length(bufferPoint - cameraPosition.xyz);
        const float sampleDistance = length(samplePoint - cameraPosition.xyz);
        const bool inFront = sampleDistance < bufferDistance;
        if (prevInFront && !inFront)
        {
            const float behind = sampleDistance - bufferDistance;
            if (behind > thickness + 0.05 * sampleDistance)
            {
                return false; // flew past a surface the stride undersampled
            }
            // Bisect between the last in-front sample and this one: the
            // crossing lands on the buffered surface, not stride-depth past it.
            float lo = tPrev;
            float hi = t;
            for (uint refine = 0u; refine < refineSteps; ++refine)
            {
                const float mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi);
                const vec3 midPoint = origin + direction * mid;
                const vec4 midClip = viewProjection * vec4(midPoint, 1.0);
                if (midClip.w <= 0.0)
                {
                    break;
                }
                const vec2 midUv = midClip.xy / midClip.w * 0.5 + 0.5;
                const float midDepth = texture(depthSampler, midUv).r;
                const vec3 midBuffer = worldPositionFromDepth(inverseViewProjection,
                                                              midUv * 2.0 - vec2(1.0), midDepth);
                if (length(midPoint - cameraPosition.xyz) < length(midBuffer - cameraPosition.xyz))
                {
                    lo = mid;
                }
                else
                {
                    hi = mid;
                }
            }
            hitPoint = origin + direction * hi;
            const vec4 hitClip = viewProjection * vec4(hitPoint, 1.0);
            hitUv = hitClip.xy / hitClip.w * 0.5 + 0.5;
            hitNormal = normalize(texture(normalSampler, hitUv).xyz);
            return true;
        }
        tPrev = t;
        prevInFront = inFront;
    }
    return false; // the march exhausted its budget: the world stage answers
}

// ---- short-range occlusion (rev 33, the Lumen ShortRangeAO analogue) -----
// A ring of depth taps around the pixel, applied AFTER the temporal filter
// (Lumen applies its shortest-range occlusion there so it carries no lag).
// Each tap that shows geometry at least the 5 cm contact band nearer than
// this surface occludes proportionally to the relative depth difference.
// The darkening is capped at 75% - a contact shadow, never a black halo.
float shortRangeOcclusion(vec2 uv, float viewDepth, uint radiusPx, float strength)
{
    const ivec2 resolution = imageSize(giImage);
    const vec2 texel = 1.0 / vec2(resolution);
    const vec2 ring[8] = vec2[8](
        vec2(-1.0, -1.0), vec2(0.0, -1.0), vec2(1.0, -1.0),
        vec2(-1.0,  0.0),                  vec2(1.0,  0.0),
        vec2(-1.0,  1.0), vec2(0.0,  1.0), vec2(1.0,  1.0));
    float occlusion = 0.0;
    uint samples = 0u;
    for (uint tap = 0u; tap < 8u; ++tap)
    {
        const vec2 tapUv = uv + ring[tap] * float(radiusPx) * texel;
        if (any(lessThan(tapUv, vec2(0.0))) || any(greaterThan(tapUv, vec2(1.0))))
        {
            continue;
        }
        const float tapDepth = texture(depthSampler, tapUv).r;
        if (tapDepth >= 1.0)
        {
            continue; // sky beside the surface cannot occlude it
        }
        const vec3 tapPoint = worldPositionFromDepth(inverseViewProjection, tapUv * 2.0 - vec2(1.0), tapDepth);
        const float tapDistance = length(tapPoint - cameraPosition.xyz);
        // Nearer geometry inside the ring, past the contact band: occlude.
        const float nearer = viewDepth - tapDistance;
        occlusion += max(nearer - 0.05, 0.0) / max(viewDepth, 0.5);
        ++samples;
    }
    if (samples == 0u)
    {
        return 1.0;
    }
    occlusion = occlusion / float(samples) * strength;
    return 1.0 - clamp(occlusion, 0.0, 0.75);
}

void main()
{
    const ivec2 pixel = ivec2(gl_GlobalInvocationID.xy);
    const ivec2 resolution = imageSize(giImage);
    if (pixel.x >= resolution.x || pixel.y >= resolution.y)
    {
        return;
    }
    const vec2 uv = (vec2(pixel) + 0.5) / vec2(resolution);
    const float depth = texture(depthSampler, uv).r;
    if (depth >= 1.0)
    {
        // Sky pixels carry no GI term (the composite's sky branch ignores this
        // target); the alpha stays a valid "sky" sentinel for the confidence
        // checks above. 60000 is the largest value RGBA16F stores exactly
        // (half-float max 65504): real view depths never approach it inside
        // the 20 km far plane, so the sentinel is unambiguous.
        imageStore(giImage, pixel, vec4(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 60000.0));
        return;
    }
    const uint primitiveCount = giPush.counts.x;
    const float frameIndex = float(giPush.counts.y);
    // The noise phase the interceptNoise draws read: the real frame counter
    // while animated_jitter is on, frozen at 0 when it is off (a
    // deterministic capture). Freezing the PHASE must not freeze the
    // temporal frame counter below - the history blend and the second-bounce
    // guard still need the real frame index.
    float noisePhase = frameIndex;
    const uint rayCount = uint(clamp(giPush.params.z, 1.0, 8.0) + 0.5);
    const uint strideSteps = uint(clamp(giPush.params2.x, 1.0, 64.0) + 0.5);
    const uint refineSteps = uint(clamp(giPush.params2.w, 1.0, 8.0) + 0.5);
    const float screenThickness = max(giPush.params2.y, 0.01);
    const bool screenTracesOn = giPush.flags.x != 0u;
    const bool jitterAnimated = giPush.flags.y != 0u;
    const float normalRejection = giPush.flags.z != 0u ? 1.0 : 0.0;
    const uint aoRadius = min(giPush.flags.w, 16u);
    const float aoStrength = max(giPush.params3.y, 0.0);
    const float temporalCap = max(giPush.params3.x, 1.0);
    const float outputIntensity = max(giPush.params3.z, 0.0);
    const float skyScale = max(giPush.params3.w, 0.0);
    if (!jitterAnimated)
    {
        noisePhase = 0.0; // frozen noise phase: a deterministic capture
    }
    const vec3 worldPosition = worldPositionFromDepth(inverseViewProjection, uv * 2.0 - vec2(1.0), depth);
    const vec3 normal = normalize(texture(normalSampler, uv).xyz);
    const float viewDepth = length(worldPosition - cameraPosition.xyz);

    // ---- the final gather: stratified cosine-distributed rays ------------
    vec3 tangent;
    vec3 bitangent;
    onb(normal, tangent, bitangent);

    vec3 gatherSum = vec3(0.0);
    for (uint ray = 0u; ray < rayCount; ++ray)
    {
        // Stratified jitter: the ray index rotates the noise domain by the
        // golden-angle conjugate so the per-pixel samples cover the cosine
        // hemisphere instead of clustering (rev 30's single sample printed
        // the lattice the denoise spent its budget fighting). The +17.31
        // frame shift decorrelates the two dimensions.
        const float rayShift = float(ray) * 2.39996322973;
        const float r1 = interceptNoise(vec2(pixel) + vec2(rayShift, -rayShift), noisePhase);
        const float r2 = interceptNoise(vec2(pixel) + vec2(53.7, 91.3) + vec2(-rayShift, rayShift), noisePhase + 17.31);
        const float angle = 6.28318530718 * r2;
        const float radius = sqrt(max(r1, 0.0));
        const vec3 direction = normalize(tangent * (radius * cos(angle)) + bitangent * (radius * sin(angle))
                                         + normal * sqrt(max(1.0 - r1, 0.0)));

        vec3 gi;
        // The ray origin rides 2 cm above the surface; the world stage
        // additionally exits whatever contains it BEFORE marching - the
        // occluder proxies wrap every mesh instance in its bounding box,
        // and a smooth body (the organic characters, the rounded canopies)
        // sits strictly INSIDE its proxy. Without this escape every
        // character pixel's gather ray reported an immediate hit against its
        // own shell (the SDF is negative inside it) and the whole crowd
        // gathered ZERO indirect light - the shaded sides read as
        // silhouettes no matter what the ambient did. The same march-out
        // softShadow uses (three overlaps max, 2 cm clearance past the last
        // face): the proxy still shades the ground around its owner, other
        // occluders still shade the owner, and the owner's shell stops
        // killing its own rays.
        const vec3 rayOrigin = worldPosition + normal * 0.02;
        vec3 incoming = vec3(0.0);
        vec3 hitAlbedo = vec3(0.0);
        vec3 hitPoint = vec3(0.0);
        vec3 hitNormal = normal;
        bool hitSurface = false;
        // ---- stage 1: the screen march (the rasterized truth) ------------
        // screen_trace = 0 skips the stage entirely: every ray goes to the
        // world stage (the world-only A/B, Lumen's Screen Traces off).
        if (screenTracesOn)
        {
            vec3 screenHitPoint;
            vec2 screenHitUv;
            vec3 screenHitNormal;
            if (screenMarch(rayOrigin, direction, primitiveCount, giPush.params.x,
                            strideSteps, refineSteps, screenThickness,
                            screenHitPoint, screenHitUv, screenHitNormal))
            {
                hitSurface = true;
                hitPoint = screenHitPoint;
                hitNormal = screenHitNormal;
                // The screen hit's material: if the point lies on an analytic
                // primitive (the chamber, the terrain) the owned relight gives
                // the full textured + emissive answer - the emissive panels keep
                // their light through this path. A mesh surface (characters,
                // props, cottages) has no analytic record: the G-buffer carries
                // the rasterized material instead (meshes are non-emissive in
                // the current content set). Either way the indirect clamp holds
                // a rare bright hit from printing a firefly the spatial filter
                // cannot average away.
                if (abs(sceneSDF(hitPoint, primitiveCount)) < 0.05)
                {
                    uint screenOwner;
                    sceneSDFOwned(hitPoint, primitiveCount, screenOwner);
                    incoming = min(surfaceOutgoingRadianceOwned(hitPoint, screenHitNormal, screenOwner, primitiveCount, hitAlbedo),
                                   vec3(max(giPush.params.w, 0.0)));
                }
                else
                {
                    hitAlbedo = texture(albedoSampler, screenHitUv).rgb;
                    incoming = min(hitAlbedo * directIrradianceOverPi(hitPoint, screenHitNormal, primitiveCount),
                                   vec3(max(giPush.params.w, 0.0)));
                }
            }
        }
        if (!hitSurface)
        {
            // ---- stage 2: the world-space fallback (the exact SDF) --------
            vec3 origin = rayOrigin;
            for (uint exit = 0u; exit < 3u; ++exit)
            {
                const float insideDepth = sceneSDF(origin, primitiveCount);
                if (insideDepth >= 0.0)
                {
                    break;
                }
                origin += direction * (-insideDepth + 0.02);
            }
            uint owner;
            const float hit = traceIntervalOwned(origin, direction, 0.02, giPush.params.x, primitiveCount,
                                                 giPush.counts.z, owner);
            if (hit >= 0.0)
            {
                hitSurface = true;
                hitPoint = origin + direction * hit;
                hitNormal = sdfNormal(hitPoint, primitiveCount);
                // The hit's own direct radiance (textured, shadowed sun + points +
                // emissive) - the "surface cache" read.
                incoming = min(surfaceOutgoingRadianceOwned(hitPoint, hitNormal, owner, primitiveCount, hitAlbedo),
                               vec3(max(giPush.params.w, 0.0)));
            }
        }
        if (hitSurface)
        {
            // The second bounce: the previous frame's gathered irradiance AT the
            // hit point, albedo-weighted (outgoing = albedo * irradiance/pi) and
            // confidence-gated by the stored depth. This is the radiance-cache
            // stand-in: one fetch, one bounce of memory, converges with the same
            // temporal filter the pixel itself uses. Frame 0 has no history to
            // read (the image's first layout transition leaves its contents
            // undefined) - the rev-30 first frame blended 12.5% of that garbage.
            // Shared by BOTH hit classes: a screen hit point is a world point
            // like any other.
            if (giPush.counts.w != 0u && frameIndex > 0.5)
            {
                const vec2 prevHitUv = previousUv(hitPoint);
                if (prevHitUv.x >= 0.0)
                {
                    const float predicted = length(hitPoint - previousCamera.cameraPosition.xyz);
                    incoming += hitAlbedo * texture(historySampler, prevHitUv).rgb
                                * historyConfidence(prevHitUv, predicted, hitNormal, normalRejection);
                }
            }
            gi = incoming;
        }
        else
        {
            // A miss really is sky: the SDF covers the scene everywhere, so the
            // ray left all geometry. skyBase is the documented GI-grade sky model
            // (gradient + dusk + broad halo + clouds, no disks - the sun and moon
            // DISKS belong to the direct pass's shadowed keys; their energy would
            // otherwise be counted twice through the same aperture).
            // sky_miss_scale shapes the miss energy (an art-direction dial: 0
            // removes sky bounce, >1 floods the indirect term with skylight).
            gi = skyBase(direction) * skyScale;
            // The moon's soft halo rides the night sky (its disk's direct light is
            // the A-186 key's business).
            if (environment.moonDirectionIntensity.w > 0.0)
            {
                const vec3 moonDirection = normalize(environment.moonDirectionIntensity.xyz);
                const float cosine = clamp(dot(direction, moonDirection), 0.0, 1.0);
                gi += vec3(0.55, 0.62, 0.80) * environment.moonDirectionIntensity.w * 0.02 * pow(cosine, 24.0) * skyScale;
            }
        }
        gatherSum += gi;
    }

    vec3 gi = gatherSum / float(rayCount);

    // ---- temporal accumulation -------------------------------------------
    // The alpha floor keeps interactive motion responsive; the running-average
    // ramp (alpha -> 1 - 1/(N+1) while N is small) lets static cameras converge
    // quadratically: the capture rig's tens of frames drive the residual noise
    // to a few percent. Rev 33: the ramp is CAPPED at temporal_max_frames
    // (Lumen's MaxFramesAccumulated, default 10 there, 64 here) - an uncapped
    // ramp hardens the history into a frozen average that stops tracking the
    // scene. Reprojection + depth/normal confidence gate the history: when the
    // camera moves, pixels whose surface identity changed fall back to the
    // fresh estimate. Frame 0 skips the blend entirely (no defined history).
    const float rampAlpha = min(1.0 - 1.0 / (frameIndex + 1.0), temporalCap / (temporalCap + 1.0));
    const float alpha = max(giPush.params.y, rampAlpha);
    const vec2 prevUv = previousUv(worldPosition);
    if (prevUv.x >= 0.0 && frameIndex > 0.5)
    {
        const float predicted = length(worldPosition - previousCamera.cameraPosition.xyz);
        const float confidence = historyConfidence(prevUv, predicted, normal, normalRejection);
        gi = mix(gi, texture(historySampler, prevUv).rgb, confidence * alpha);
    }

    // ---- short-range occlusion (post-temporal, Lumen's ordering) ---------
    if (aoRadius > 0u)
    {
        gi *= shortRangeOcclusion(uv, viewDepth, aoRadius, aoStrength);
    }

    // ---- output shaping ----------------------------------------------------
    // intensity scales the STORED term at the last moment - the history keeps
    // the unscaled transport (the second-bounce read stays consistent: every
    // frame's output is intensity * (gather + bounce), never intensity^2).
    gi *= outputIntensity;

    // Alpha = view depth: the confidence metric both temporal consumers share.
    imageStore(giImage, pixel, vec4(gi, viewDepth));
}
